    <section class="offset-tech-card offset-tech-card--numbers" aria-label="Wheel offset explanation">
      <header><strong>What changed</strong><span>NUMBER → SHAPE → MEANING</span></header>
      <svg class="offset-mini-stance" viewBox="0 0 300 128" role="img" aria-label="Top view showing current and new outer wheel positions">
        <path class="offset-mini-body" d="M78 20h144l36 29v42l-36 17H78L42 91V49Z"/>
        <path class="offset-mini-center" d="M150 13v102"/>
        <rect class="offset-mini-wheel offset-mini-wheel--current" data-current-mini-wheel x="202" y="31" width="30" height="68" rx="8"/>
        <rect class="offset-mini-wheel offset-mini-wheel--new" data-new-mini-wheel x="212" y="31" width="34" height="68" rx="8"/>
        <path class="offset-mini-arrow" data-mini-outer-arrow d="M232 110H246"/>
        <text data-mini-outer-text x="239" y="124" text-anchor="middle">+11.4 mm</text>
      </svg>
      <div class="offset-tech-values">
        <div><span>Original</span><strong data-original-wheel-spec>8J · ET40</strong></div>
        <div><span>New</span><strong data-new-wheel-spec>8.5J · ET35</strong></div>
        <div><span>Inner edge</span><strong data-inner-value>+1.35 mm</strong><small data-inner-copy>farther inward</small></div>
        <div><span>Outer edge</span><strong data-outer-value>+11.35 mm</strong><small data-outer-copy>farther outward</small></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="offset-tech-note"><strong>Read the drawing like a cutaway</strong><p>The mounting face does not move. Width and ET move the wheel body around that fixed plane. This is wheel geometry, not a brake/tire/fender fitment verdict.</p></aside>
    </section>
  </div>
